[statement]
A preliminary choice made for a name walked first does not steer a name
some package carries that the request names: `d`, requested and walked
before `f`, has `f` 2 as its best candidate, providing it at 2; `f`
takes its own best candidate, `f` 3, which answers `d` at 1, and apk
installs `f` 3 alone. A name required only through other packages takes
the package chosen already (`a-name-a-choice-answers-takes-that-package`).
The rule is known only in part: in some shapes apk still takes the
earlier choice for a requested name.

[repository]
P:f
V:3
p:d=1

P:f
V:2
p:d=2

[request]
d
f

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install f 3
